      choices: [
        `Remained at $10.`,
        `Was reduced to $8.`,
        `Was reduced to $5.`,
        `Was reduced to $2.`,
      ],
      correctIndex: 3,
      explanation: `<div style="border-radius:10px; box-shadow:0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; overflow:hidden"><div style="background-color:#01506e; border-radius:8px 8px 0 0; color:white; padding:20px"><h1 style="color:white; margin:0">Stock Split Accounting</h1></div><div style="background-color:white; padding:20px"><div style="background-color:#f9f9f9; border-left:5px solid #0099d4; border-radius:8px; margin-bottom:20px; padding:15px"><h3 style="color:#01506e; margin:0 0 12px 0">Correct Answer</h3><p style="margin:0"><span style="color:#4caf50; font-weight:bold">✓</span> <span style="color:#4caf50; font-weight:bold">Was reduced to $2.</span></p></div><div style="background-color:#f0f7fa; border-left:5px solid #68d3a7; border-radius:8px; margin-bottom:20px; padding:15px"><p style="margin:0">Question: After the 5-for-1 stock split, the par value of the stock:</p></div><div style="background-color:#f9f9f9; border-left:5px solid #0099d4; border-radius:8px; margin-bottom:20px; padding:15px"><h3 style="color:#01506e; margin:0 0 12px 0">Explanation</h3><p style="margin:0">In a stock split, the par value of the stock is adjusted proportionally to maintain the same total par value. For a 5-for-1 stock split, the par value is divided by 5.</p><ul style="margin:0 0 12px 0; padding-left:22px"><li style="margin:0 0 8px 0">Original par value: $10</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px 0">Stock split ratio: 5-for-1</li></ul><div style="background-color:white; border:1px solid #dddddd; border-radius:5px; color:#12232d; font-family:monospace; margin:0 0 12px 0; padding:12px; text-align:center"><strong>New par value calculation: $10 ÷ 5 = $2</strong></div></div><div style="background-color:#f5f9fc; border-left:5px solid #207bb5; border-radius:8px; margin-bottom:20px; padding:15px"><h3 style="color:#01506e; margin:0 0 12px 0">Analysis</h3><div style="background-color:white; border:1px solid #dddddd; border-radius:5px; color:#12232d; font-family:monospace; margin:0 0 12px 0; padding:12px; text-align:center"><strong>Before the split: 10,000 shares at $10 par value = $100,000 total par value</strong></div><div style="background-color:white; border:1px solid #dddddd; border-radius:5px; color:#12232d; font-family:monospace; margin:0 0 12px 0; padding:12px; text-align:center"><strong>After the split: 50,000 shares (10,000 × 5) at $2 par value = $100,000 total par value</strong></div><p style="margin:0">Total par value remains unchanged, only distributed across more shares</p></div><div style="background-color:#01506e; border-radius:0 0 8px 8px; color:white; padding:15px"><h3 style="color:white; margin:0 0 12px 0">Summary</h3><p style="margin:0">In a stock split, the par value of shares is adjusted in inverse proportion to the split ratio. In this 5-for-1 stock split, the par value decreased from $10 to $2, while the number of shares increased from 10,000 to 50,000. The total par value and total stockholders&#x27; equity remain unchanged.</p></div></div></div>`,
